WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.620
We're on the record this morning.

00:03.620 --> 00:08.940
This is Idaho County case number CR 25-25-1933,

00:08.940 --> 00:11.280
State of Idaho versus William Smith.

00:11.280 --> 00:13.720
Mr. Smith is personally present in the courtroom today,

00:13.720 --> 00:15.400
along with his attorney, Mr. Gluzak.

00:15.400 --> 00:17.640
State of Idaho is represented by Mr. Kurt McGregor,

00:17.640 --> 00:19.120
prosecuting attorney for Idaho County,

00:19.120 --> 00:21.760
who is also personally present in the courtroom today.

00:21.760 --> 00:23.840
Except for a status conference today,

00:23.840 --> 00:27.200
but Mr. Gluzak's filed a motion to withdraw

00:27.360 --> 00:30.720
from his representation of Mr. Smith in this matter.

00:30.720 --> 00:33.840
I have reviewed that motion.

00:33.840 --> 00:35.960
Mr. McGregor, did you have an objection?

00:35.960 --> 00:37.280
I do not, Joe.

00:37.280 --> 00:38.520
Mr. Smith, do you understand

00:38.520 --> 00:40.880
that Mr. Gluzak's filed a motion to withdraw in this matter?

00:40.880 --> 00:41.720
Yeah.

00:41.720 --> 00:42.560
And do you object?

00:42.560 --> 00:43.400
No.

00:43.400 --> 00:44.240
You have no objection?

00:44.240 --> 00:45.080
No.

00:45.080 --> 00:45.920
Okay.

00:45.920 --> 00:48.200
Mr. Smith, is it your intention to represent yourself

00:48.200 --> 00:49.800
going forward in this matter?

00:49.800 --> 00:51.120
For right now, yes.

00:51.120 --> 00:52.120
For right now?

00:52.120 --> 00:53.360
Okay.

00:53.360 --> 00:55.480
Mr. Gluzak, any arguments you wanna make

00:55.520 --> 00:57.520
in supporting your motion to withdraw?

00:57.520 --> 01:02.240
Just, I think that it very clearly constitutes a conflict,

01:02.240 --> 01:05.320
puts us in an adverse position given what was discussed

01:05.320 --> 01:07.560
in that filing and I would ask the court to grant a motion.

01:07.560 --> 01:08.920
Okay.

01:08.920 --> 01:13.160
Mr. Smith, before I allow Mr. Gluzak to withdraw,

01:13.160 --> 01:14.680
we need to discuss your ability

01:14.680 --> 01:17.040
to represent yourself in this matter.

01:17.040 --> 01:18.960
Mr. Smith, are you able to read and write

01:18.960 --> 01:19.920
the English language?

01:19.920 --> 01:20.760
Yeah.

01:20.760 --> 01:21.600
Okay.

01:21.600 --> 01:22.440
And did you complete high school?

01:22.440 --> 01:23.280
No.

01:23.280 --> 01:24.960
What's the highest level of education

01:24.960 --> 01:26.320
you've reached, Mr. Smith?

01:26.320 --> 01:27.240
11th grade.

01:27.240 --> 01:28.080
11th grade?

01:28.080 --> 01:28.900
Okay.

01:28.900 --> 01:30.840
Mr. Smith, do you have any training in the law?

01:30.840 --> 01:31.680
No.

01:33.680 --> 01:37.760
Mr. Smith, you have filed some documents in this matter

01:37.760 --> 01:40.840
which I have reviewed and based upon my review,

01:40.840 --> 01:45.200
they don't appear to conform to the court rules.

01:45.200 --> 01:47.120
You understand that if you represent yourself

01:47.120 --> 01:51.040
in this matter that your representation is going to be

01:51.040 --> 01:53.520
required to comply to the court rules.

01:55.960 --> 01:57.640
Do you understand that, Mr. Smith?

01:57.640 --> 01:58.480
Yes.

01:58.480 --> 01:59.320
Okay.

01:59.320 --> 02:01.520
And Mr. Smith, how are you going to ensure

02:01.520 --> 02:03.920
that your filing is complied with the court rules?

02:05.360 --> 02:07.400
I'll probably just have to hire an attorney.

02:07.400 --> 02:08.240
Okay.

02:08.240 --> 02:10.880
So it would be your intention to hire your own attorney?

02:10.880 --> 02:11.720
Okay.

02:11.720 --> 02:14.240
If that is your intention and how you want to proceed,

02:14.240 --> 02:17.560
that is certainly fine but there's going to be this interim

02:17.560 --> 02:19.960
where you represent yourself and I want to make sure

02:19.960 --> 02:22.280
that you can adequately do so.

02:22.280 --> 02:23.760
Does that make sense?

02:23.760 --> 02:26.520
You understand that you have a constitutional right

02:26.520 --> 02:28.440
to be represented by an attorney?

02:28.440 --> 02:29.280
Yeah.

02:29.280 --> 02:30.120
Okay.

02:30.120 --> 02:32.800
So under the sixth amendment of the U.S. Constitution,

02:32.800 --> 02:34.520
you have the right to be represented

02:34.520 --> 02:37.200
at all stages of these proceedings

02:37.200 --> 02:40.120
and that if you allow Mr. Gluzak to withdraw

02:40.120 --> 02:42.600
from his representation, you're not going to be represented

02:42.600 --> 02:45.360
until you hire a new attorney, understand that?

02:45.360 --> 02:46.200
Okay.

02:49.320 --> 02:51.880
If you can't afford an attorney,

02:51.880 --> 02:54.080
I will point one at public expense,

02:54.080 --> 02:56.160
just like Mr. Gluzak has.

02:56.160 --> 02:57.800
You understand that?

02:57.800 --> 03:01.440
Can we do that then until I can figure out what's going on?

03:01.440 --> 03:03.960
Well, so you would like to be represented by an attorney

03:03.960 --> 03:07.000
just a different attorney than Mr. Gluzak, is that correct?

03:07.000 --> 03:07.840
Okay.

03:07.840 --> 03:08.840
And the reason you don't want to be represented

03:08.840 --> 03:11.720
by Mr. Gluzak any longer is what, Mr. Smith?

03:12.720 --> 03:13.560
We filed.

03:13.560 --> 03:15.400
We filed something.

03:15.400 --> 03:16.800
Who's we, Mr. Smith?

03:16.800 --> 03:18.320
Oh, I did.

03:18.320 --> 03:19.160
I filed.

03:19.160 --> 03:21.200
You filed what?

03:21.200 --> 03:22.360
I lost it again, sir.

03:22.360 --> 03:25.160
You filed a lawsuit against Mr. Gluzak?

03:25.160 --> 03:28.840
And I would ask for a recusal from you because...

03:28.840 --> 03:30.600
You're not getting a recusal from me, Mr. Smith.

03:30.600 --> 03:32.400
I mean, well, I filed a tort claim against you.

03:32.400 --> 03:33.720
I don't care.

03:33.720 --> 03:35.040
I'm still going to sit on your case

03:35.040 --> 03:36.680
and be your judge, Mr. Smith.

03:38.680 --> 03:40.960
So why did you sue Mr. Gluzak?

03:42.520 --> 03:44.320
I got some people here if you want to read it.

03:44.320 --> 03:45.600
I don't want to read your paperwork.

03:45.600 --> 03:47.600
I'm asking you, Mr. Smith,

03:47.600 --> 03:50.040
why did you sue Mr. Gluzak?

03:51.640 --> 03:52.960
I don't want to see it.

03:54.840 --> 03:56.680
Bam.

03:56.680 --> 04:00.240
Suppression of evidence, a ban.

04:00.240 --> 04:02.600
I don't understand what that means, Mr. Smith.

04:02.600 --> 04:06.000
What do you allege Mr. Gluzak did

04:06.000 --> 04:08.760
that caused you to file a lawsuit against him?

04:08.760 --> 04:10.760
Yes, dude, you'll have to read this.

04:10.760 --> 04:12.040
I'm not going to read it, Mr. Smith.

04:12.040 --> 04:14.040
I'm asking you to tell me.

04:15.120 --> 04:16.440
I'm not really sure.

04:16.440 --> 04:17.280
I don't know.

04:17.280 --> 04:18.120
My mom's the one filing it.

04:18.120 --> 04:20.360
Your mom filed a lawsuit on your behalf

04:20.360 --> 04:21.320
against your attorney.

04:21.320 --> 04:22.600
I'm trying, yes.

04:22.600 --> 04:23.720
Okay.

04:23.720 --> 04:25.920
So you don't make the allegations in the lawsuit.

04:25.920 --> 04:27.200
Is that correct, Mr. Smith?

04:27.200 --> 04:28.040
I did, yes.

04:28.040 --> 04:29.920
You did make the allegations?

04:29.920 --> 04:30.760
I don't know.

04:32.800 --> 04:33.640
I don't know.

04:33.640 --> 04:34.480
You don't know?

04:34.480 --> 04:35.320
I don't know what you're going to say.

04:35.320 --> 04:36.480
I'm trying to read this to you.

04:36.480 --> 04:37.640
I don't want you to read it to me.

04:37.640 --> 04:39.560
I want you to tell me, Mr. Smith,

04:39.560 --> 04:42.360
why did you sue Mr. Gluzak?

04:42.360 --> 04:43.640
I just told you.

04:43.640 --> 04:44.480
Why?

04:44.480 --> 04:46.520
For abandonment, professional misconduct,

04:46.520 --> 04:49.960
failure to act, abandonment of defense.

04:50.000 --> 04:51.200
What does that mean?

04:52.760 --> 04:55.240
Everything, he's just not finning me the way he should.

04:55.240 --> 04:58.280
So why would I appoint another attorney

04:58.280 --> 05:00.280
who you can then make the same allegations

05:00.280 --> 05:01.840
against Mr. Smith?

05:01.840 --> 05:04.840
I wouldn't know if, I wouldn't make the same allegations.

05:06.080 --> 05:08.960
You don't know if you'd make the same allegations?

05:08.960 --> 05:11.760
I wouldn't know because I haven't got represented by them.

05:11.760 --> 05:16.760
I am not going to tolerate you abusing counsel

05:17.040 --> 05:18.640
in this matter, Mr. Smith.

05:18.640 --> 05:20.640
I made this point last time.

05:20.640 --> 05:22.160
Okay, do you understand that?

05:22.160 --> 05:24.360
You are not going to abuse your counsel.

05:24.360 --> 05:28.000
And if you do, you are going to forfeit your right

05:28.000 --> 05:30.200
to be represented by counsel.

05:30.200 --> 05:31.760
Do you understand that?

05:31.760 --> 05:34.920
And that includes filing frivolous lawsuits

05:34.920 --> 05:36.840
against your counsel, Mr. Smith.

05:36.840 --> 05:38.360
Do you understand that?

05:38.360 --> 05:40.120
I would just hire my own attorney.

05:41.280 --> 05:43.240
Do you want to hire your own attorney?

05:43.240 --> 05:45.360
Do you have the funds to hire an attorney?

05:45.360 --> 05:47.040
Who are you going to hire, Mr. Smith?

05:47.040 --> 05:48.920
I'm going to make some phone calls.

05:48.920 --> 05:50.280
You haven't thought about this

05:50.280 --> 05:52.960
until this point today, Mr. Smith?

05:52.960 --> 05:56.240
No, I've been in and out of the hospital, I've been sick.

05:58.440 --> 06:00.320
How much time do you need

06:00.320 --> 06:02.400
to hire your own attorney, Mr. Smith?

06:04.000 --> 06:05.080
Maybe a couple weeks.

06:05.080 --> 06:06.280
Two weeks?

06:06.280 --> 06:07.360
Is that sufficient?

06:10.760 --> 06:12.320
What am I going to do, Mr. Smith,

06:12.320 --> 06:14.960
if you don't hire your own attorney in two weeks?

06:17.040 --> 06:17.880
I don't know.

06:47.040 --> 06:57.280
Madam clerk, do we have time on May 11th

06:57.280 --> 06:59.320
for status conference, Mr. Smith?

07:05.040 --> 07:08.600
We have time in the afternoon at 3.30.

07:08.600 --> 07:09.600
3.30?

07:09.600 --> 07:12.960
Mr. Gluzak, are you available on May 11th at 3.30?

07:14.000 --> 07:15.200
I am.

07:15.200 --> 07:17.240
You can appear by Zoom, Mr. Gluzak.

07:17.240 --> 07:19.360
Mr. Greger, May 11th at 3.30?

07:19.360 --> 07:20.640
I'm available, Jeff.

07:20.640 --> 07:23.360
Mr. Smith, May 11th at 3.30?

07:23.360 --> 07:24.680
All right, I'm going to set this matter

07:24.680 --> 07:27.880
for a status conference, May 11th at 3.30.

07:27.880 --> 07:31.880
I am going to not grant Mr. Gluzak's motion

07:31.880 --> 07:33.880
to withdraw at this time

07:33.880 --> 07:35.280
and give you those two weeks

07:35.280 --> 07:38.080
to hire your own counsel, Mr. Smith.

07:38.080 --> 07:40.120
If you do not hire your own counsel

07:40.120 --> 07:43.720
by May 11th at 3.30 when I see you next,

07:43.720 --> 07:47.000
I will consider allowing Mr. Gluzak to withdraw

07:47.000 --> 07:49.120
and we will discuss whether you're going to proceed

07:49.120 --> 07:50.640
representing yourself at that point.

07:50.640 --> 07:52.000
Do you understand that?

07:52.000 --> 07:54.200
Do you understand that I'm not going to tolerate

07:54.200 --> 07:58.040
any abuse of your counsel, Mr. Smith?

07:58.040 --> 07:59.960
I'm not going to tolerate your mom

07:59.960 --> 08:02.120
abusing your counsel, Mr. Smith.

08:02.120 --> 08:03.760
I think there's a very high likelihood

08:03.760 --> 08:05.440
your mother committed a crime

08:05.440 --> 08:08.320
by filing that lawsuit on your behalf, Mr. Smith.

08:08.320 --> 08:09.520
Do you understand that?

08:10.480 --> 08:11.320
I've been...

08:11.320 --> 08:13.200
Do you understand that, Mr. Smith?

08:13.200 --> 08:14.040
Yeah.

08:14.040 --> 08:17.080
Okay, it's not going to be tolerated in this court.

08:17.080 --> 08:18.720
Other things that are not going to be tolerated

08:18.720 --> 08:21.960
in this court, Mr. Smith, are abusing court staff.

08:21.960 --> 08:24.440
You are not to go to the window

08:24.440 --> 08:27.800
and film court staff any longer, Mr. Smith.

08:27.800 --> 08:29.000
Do you understand that?

08:29.000 --> 08:30.160
I haven't filmed anybody.

08:30.160 --> 08:33.640
Do not film court staff, Mr. Smith.

08:33.640 --> 08:34.960
Do you understand that?

08:34.960 --> 08:35.800
I don't think they have...

08:35.800 --> 08:37.840
That is a court order, Mr. Smith,

08:37.840 --> 08:39.680
and if you violate that court order,

08:39.680 --> 08:41.120
you will be in contempt of this court

08:41.120 --> 08:42.840
and I will have you placed in jail.

08:42.840 --> 08:44.280
Do you understand that, Mr. Smith?

08:44.280 --> 08:45.120
Yes, but I...

08:45.120 --> 08:47.640
You are not to direct anybody on your behalf

08:47.640 --> 08:50.120
to film court staff, Mr. Smith.

08:50.120 --> 08:51.160
Do you understand that?

08:51.160 --> 08:52.920
I mean, nobody recorded it.

08:52.920 --> 08:55.720
Mr. Smith, I'm not asking whether it happened.

08:55.720 --> 08:57.080
I'm telling you right now

08:57.080 --> 08:59.720
it's not going to happen in the future.

08:59.720 --> 09:01.600
Do you understand?

09:01.600 --> 09:04.600
Anybody who acts in concert with you

09:04.600 --> 09:07.680
to harass your counsel or court staff

09:07.680 --> 09:10.280
will be in contempt of this court and will deal with me.

09:10.280 --> 09:12.440
Do you understand that, Mr. Smith?

09:12.440 --> 09:14.120
Do you think I am going to be friendly

09:14.120 --> 09:16.360
to those people, Mr. Smith?

09:16.360 --> 09:17.200
I'm not.

09:17.200 --> 09:18.040
Probably not.

09:20.480 --> 09:24.440
I am very displeased, Mr. Smith,

09:24.440 --> 09:26.720
if you did not guess by the tone of my voice.

09:29.240 --> 09:34.240
You are not going to harass this system any longer, Mr. Smith.

09:34.440 --> 09:36.480
Any longer, Mr. Smith.

09:36.480 --> 09:39.560
And anybody who acts on your behalf will answer to me.

09:40.560 --> 09:41.400
Understood?

09:42.680 --> 09:43.520
Yes?

09:43.520 --> 09:44.360
Yes.

09:44.360 --> 09:45.200
Okay.

09:45.200 --> 09:47.680
You have two weeks to retain your own counsel, Mr. Smith.

09:47.680 --> 09:50.840
If you do not do so, we will discuss how we proceed.

09:50.840 --> 09:53.000
I'm not going to extend any deadlines.

09:53.000 --> 09:55.480
Your trial date will remain as it's set.

09:55.480 --> 09:56.440
Do you understand that?

09:56.440 --> 09:57.520
Yes.

09:57.520 --> 09:59.240
Do you have any questions?

09:59.240 --> 10:00.520
Anything further you want to address

10:00.520 --> 10:02.360
in this matter today, Mr. Gluzak?

10:02.360 --> 10:03.440
No, Your Honor, thank you.

10:03.440 --> 10:04.680
Mr. McGregor?

10:04.680 --> 10:05.520
No, Your Honor.

10:05.520 --> 10:06.360
All right.

10:06.360 --> 10:07.880
Mr. Smith, you may be excused.

10:10.920 --> 10:12.240
Are you glad to do what it is?

10:12.240 --> 10:13.640
The back door, Mr. Smith.

